# TypeScript & tests

- **Strict TS.** No `any`. Prefer precise types and `readonly` where it clarifies
  intent. Let inference work internally; annotate exported/public boundaries.
- **`npm run typecheck` is the gate** — it must pass with zero errors before a
  change is done.
- **Colocate tests** as `name.test.ts` next to the module (Vitest). Run with
  `npm test`.
- **Test the pure core.** Anything in `src/core/` (movement, collision, spawn,
  expiry, damage) should have unit tests covering behavior + edge cases — not
  implementation detail. `src/view/` (Pixi) is verified visually instead.
- **Comments explain _why_, not _what_.** No narration; document intent,
  trade-offs, and non-obvious constraints.

```ts
// ❌ magic number, narration
tank.speed += 520 * dt; // add to speed

// ✅ tunable from config, intent-level comment (only when non-obvious)
tank.speed += TANK.accel * dt;
```
